                <pb facs="0423" n="299" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg299"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.7363b W 52/150: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Wheeler</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-07-18T16:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 18, 1923—4
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 6:55 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>303. My number 250, June 26, 4 p.m. On the 13th instant the Western Union
                    despatched a letter to Sir John Pender stating that in the event he did not
                    reply to the company’s offer set forth in the telegram above referred to it
                    would be withdrawn.</p>
                <p>Yesterday Sir John replied to the Western Union rejecting the offer.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wheeler</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
